{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "label": "Behaviors namespace", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Combinators that build Behavior values; an actor's lifetime is a sequence of behaviors, each handler returning the next one."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_receive", "label": "Behaviors.receive", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_receivemessage", "label": "Behaviors.receiveMessage", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The shortcut for handlers that do not need the context."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_receivewithsignal", "label": "Behaviors.receiveWithSignal", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The typed equivalent of overriding postStop/preRestart and handling Terminated: post-stop, pre-restart and terminated arrive at a second handler."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_setup", "label": "Behaviors.setup", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Runs once at start for initialization the receive handler should close over - spawning children, capturing self, opening connections - and is also where a behavior names itself."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_withtimers", "label": "Behaviors.withTimers", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Captures the same TimerScheduler context.timers exposes in a closure, so the handler reaches it without going through the context on every message."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_withstash", "label": "Behaviors.withStash", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A capacity-bounded stash as a value rather than via context. unstashAll puts buffered messages back at the front of the mailbox so they precede anything that arrived while stashing, and whatever is still parked at stop or restart goes to dead letters. Two deliberate differences from the context form: capacity is per behavior, and stash(message) takes the message explicitly - which is why a dead letter minted here carries no original sender."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_supervise", "label": "Behaviors.supervise", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The restart tally belongs to the supervise wrapper rather than the strategy value, so one strategy handed to several behaviors gives each its own allowance, and only installing a new wrapper resets it. Escalating past maxRetries layers the parent's strategy instead of duplicating it: a parent-granted restart builds a fresh actor whose per-behavior allowance starts over."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_intercept", "label": "Behaviors.intercept", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Runs first on every user message and may delegate, transform or drop. The wrapper survives the inner behavior's transitions - a state machine returning a fresh behavior each message is still intercepted - and the type is T to T, so an interceptor never changes the actor's message type. Its errors reach an enclosing supervise; lifecycle signals bypass it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_monitor", "label": "Behaviors.monitor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Forwards every message to an observer before the inner behavior handles it. Forward-then-deliver is deliberate so the monitor still sees a message whose handling crashes the actor, and delivery is fire-and-forget with failures swallowed so a broken tap cannot take the actor down."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_logmessages", "label": "Behaviors.logMessages", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only debug and info levels are offered, because logging every message at warn or error would poison the signal an operator filters on. A throwing formatter falls back to the built-in line rather than killing the actor it observes, and the line is only built when the logger would actually emit it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behavior_sentinels", "label": "The five sentinels", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "same keeps the closure, stopped terminates, unhandled routes to dead letters, empty accepts but does nothing, ignore drops silently. same is also cheaper than rebuilding an equivalent receive because the runtime recognises the singleton."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_context_setdisplayname", "label": "context.setDisplayName", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every Behavior runs inside the same TypedActor class, so there is no subclass on which to override displayName(); without setDisplayName a whole tree of typed actors reports TypedActor and tells you nothing about which is which. It can be called any time, not only from setup."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_decorator_composition_order", "label": "Decorator composition order", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Decorators compose outside-in and all but the interceptors are resolved away at start - they contribute their side effect and collapse. An interceptor cannot, because it must still be there on the next message, which is also what decides whether a restart rebuilds it: inside a supervise wrapper it is rebuilt, outside it keeps observing across the restart, and either way it stays installed exactly once."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_receive", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_receivemessage", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_receivewithsignal", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_setup", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_withtimers", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_withstash", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_supervise", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_intercept", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_monitor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_logmessages", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behavior_sentinels", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_setup", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_context_setdisplayname", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_receivemessage", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_receive", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_decorator_composition_order", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_intercept", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.